@testray.main.component.name = "Support QA"
@type = "koroneiki.integration"

Feature:  Koroneiki to Provisioning Subscription Integration
	Testing to assure that koroneiki account subscription information transfers properly to the account index.

Teardown:
	* I wait for "10" seconds
	* I tear down the teams on koroneiki with the following names
	| Koroneiki Partner |
	| Updated Partner   |
	* I tear down the team roles on koroneiki with the following names
	| Partner |
	* I tear down the external links for the product "A Liferay DXP Product" on koroneiki with the following entity id values
	| A Liferay DXP Product |
	* I tear down the external links for the product "Platinum Subscription" on koroneiki with the following entity id values
	| Platinum Subscription |
	* I tear down the external links for the product "Gold Subscription" on koroneiki with the following entity id values
	| Gold Subscription |
	* I tear down the external links for the account "Korpro - ${staticCompanyName}" on koroneiki with the following entity id values
	| ${staticDossieraAccountKey}   |
	| ${staticSalesforceProjectKey} |
	* I tear down the product consumptions on koroneiki made by the account "Korpro - ${staticCompanyName}" for the following products
	| A Liferay DXP Product  |
	| Liferay DXP Production |
	| Platinum Subscription  |
	| Gold Subscription      |
	* I tear down the product consumptions on koroneiki made by the account "Onepro - ${staticCompanyName}" for the following products
	| A Liferay DXP Product  |
	| Liferay DXP Production |
	| Platinum Subscription  |
	| Gold Subscription      |
	* I tear down the product purchases on koroneiki made by the account "Korpro - ${staticCompanyName}" for the following products
	| A Liferay DXP Product  |
	| Liferay DXP Production |
	| Platinum Subscription  |
	| Gold Subscription      |
	* I tear down the product purchases on koroneiki made by the account "Onepro - ${staticCompanyName}" for the following products
	| A Liferay DXP Product  |
	| Liferay DXP Production |
	| Platinum Subscription  |
	| Gold Subscription      |
	* I tear down the products on koroneiki with the following names
	| A Liferay DXP Product |
	| Platinum Subscription |
	| Gold Subscription     |
	* I tear down the contact roles on koroneiki with the following names
	| Liferay Account Customer Role |
 	* I tear down the contacts on koroneiki with the following email addresses
	| pro.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	* I tear down the accounts on koroneiki with the following names
	| Korpro - ${staticCompanyName} |
	| Onepro - ${staticCompanyName} |
	* I tear down the accounts on koroneiki with the following "Code" values
	| KORPROKORPRO |
	| ONEPROONEPRO |

Scenario: View platinum subscription
	Testing the ability to create a platinum subcription in Dossiera and viewing the subscription in the provisioning account details page 

	Given I generate several static variables for Provisioning
	And I generate a provisioning company name
	And I generate a provisioning project name
	And I publish a project with no partner RabbitMQ message on sandbox with routing key "dossiera.provisioning.create" with the following values
	| Account Name                           | Korpro - ${staticCompanyName}              |
	| Address City                           | Diamond Bar                                |
	| Address Country                        | United States                              |
	| Address Postal Code                    | 91765                                      |
	| Address Region                         | California                                 |
	| Address Street                         | 456 Fake Street                            |
	| Contact Email Address                  | pro.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken       |
	| Contact First Name                     | PRO                                        |
	| Contact Last Name                      | Koroneiki1                                 |
	| Contact Role                           | Liferay Account Customer Role              |
	| Dossiera Account Key                   | ${staticDossieraAccountKey}                |
	| Dossiera Address Key 1                 | ${staticDossieraAddressKey1}               |
	| Dossiera Address Key 2                 | ${staticDossieraAddressKey2}               |
	| Dossiera Contact Key                   | ${staticDossieraContactKey}                |
	| Dossiera Project Key                   | ${staticDossieraProjectKey}                |
	| End Day                                | ${staticEndDay}                            |
	| End Month                              | ${staticEndMonth}                          |
	| End Year                               | ${staticEndYear}                           |
	| Industry                               | Automotive                                 |
	| Owner Email Address                    | pro.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken       |
	| Owner First Name                       | PRO                                        |
	| Owner Last Name                        | Koroneiki1                                 |
	| Partner First Line Support             | false                                      |
	| Product Type                           | New                                        |
	| Product Name                           | A Liferay DXP Product                      |
	| Project Name                           | Korpro - ${staticProjectName}              |
	| Renewal                                | false                                      |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Key             | ${staticSalesforceOpportunityKey}          |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Line Item Key 1 | ${staticSalesforceOpportunityLineItemKey1} |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Line Item Key 2 | ${staticSalesforceOpportunityLineItemKey2} |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Sold By         | Liferay US                                 |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Stage Name      | Closed Won                                 |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Territory       | United States                              |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Type            | New Business                               |
	| Salesforce Owner User Key              | ${staticSalesforceOwnerUserKey}            |
	| Salesforce Project Key                 | ${staticSalesforceProjectKey}              |
	| Start Day                              | ${staticStartDay}                          |
	| Start Month                            | ${staticStartMonth}                        |
	| Start Year                             | ${staticStartYear}                         |
	| Subscription Level                     | Platinum                                   |
	| Version Number                         | 7.1                                        |
	And I wait for "10" seconds
	And I create a product consumption for an account with the name "Korpro - ${staticCompanyName}" and the product "A Liferay DXP Product" on koroneiki with the following values
	| Product Field and Value | additionalProp1 | propertyValue1 |
	| Product Field and Value | additionalProp2 | propertyValue2 |
	| Product Field and Value | additionalProp3 | propertyValue3 |
	And I log into the provisioning homepage as "test@liferay.com" with password "kwSgiajslgb7ecsD"
	And I search the accounts page using the keyword "Korpro"
	And I click on the account with the name "Korpro - ${staticCompanyName}" on the provisioning index
	Then I should be able to view the product under the "Active" tab with the name "A Liferay DXP Product" and the following values on the account details page
	| Name         | A Liferay DXP Product |
	| Provisioned  | 1                     |
	| Purchased    | 1                     |
	| Status       | ACTIVE                |
	And I should be able to view the product under the "Active" tab with the name "Platinum Subscription" and the following values on the account details page
	| Name         | Platinum Subscription |
	| Provisioned  | 0                     |
	| Purchased    | 1                     |
	| Status       | ACTIVE                |
	When I click on the "Inactive" tab
	Then I should not be able to view the product under the "Inactive" tab with the name "A Liferay DXP Product" on the account details page
	And I should not be able to view the product under the "Inactive" tab with the name "Platinum Subscription" on the account details page
	When I click on the "All" tab
	Then I should be able to view the product under the "All" tab with the name "A Liferay DXP Product" and the following values on the account details page
	| Name         | A Liferay DXP Product |
	| Provisioned  | 1                     |
	| Purchased    | 1                     |
	| Status       | ACTIVE                |
	And I should be able to view the product under the "All" tab with the name "Platinum Subscription" and the following values on the account details page
	| Name         | Platinum Subscription |
	| Provisioned  | 0                     |
	| Purchased    | 1                     |
	| Status       | ACTIVE                |

Scenario: View non perpetual subscription
	Testing the ability to create a platinum subcription in Dossiera and updating the subscription to be non perpetual before viewing the subscription in the provisioning account details page 

	Given I generate several static variables for Provisioning
	And I generate a provisioning company name
	And I generate a provisioning project name
	And I publish a project with no partner RabbitMQ message on sandbox with routing key "dossiera.provisioning.create" with the following values
	| Account Name                           | Korpro - ${staticCompanyName}              |
	| Address City                           | Diamond Bar                                |
	| Address Country                        | United States                              |
	| Address Postal Code                    | 91765                                      |
	| Address Region                         | California                                 |
	| Address Street                         | 456 Fake Street                            |
	| Contact Email Address                  | pro.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken       |
	| Contact First Name                     | PRO                                        |
	| Contact Last Name                      | Koroneiki1                                 |
	| Contact Role                           | Liferay Account Customer Role              |
	| Dossiera Account Key                   | ${staticDossieraAccountKey}                |
	| Dossiera Address Key 1                 | ${staticDossieraAddressKey1}               |
	| Dossiera Address Key 2                 | ${staticDossieraAddressKey2}               |
	| Dossiera Contact Key                   | ${staticDossieraContactKey}                |
	| Dossiera Project Key                   | ${staticDossieraProjectKey}                |
	| End Day                                | ${staticEndDay}                            |
	| End Month                              | ${staticEndMonth}                          |
	| End Year                               | ${staticEndYear}                           |
	| Industry                               | Automotive                                 |
	| Owner Email Address                    | pro.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken       |
	| Owner First Name                       | PRO                                        |
	| Owner Last Name                        | Koroneiki1                                 |
	| Partner First Line Support             | false                                      |
	| Product Type                           | New                                        |
	| Product Name                           | A Liferay DXP Product                      |
	| Project Name                           | Korpro - ${staticProjectName}              |
	| Renewal                                | false                                      |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Key             | ${staticSalesforceOpportunityKey}          |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Line Item Key 1 | ${staticSalesforceOpportunityLineItemKey1} |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Line Item Key 2 | ${staticSalesforceOpportunityLineItemKey2} |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Sold By         | Liferay US                                 |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Stage Name      | Closed Won                                 |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Territory       | United States                              |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Type            | New Business                               |
	| Salesforce Owner User Key              | ${staticSalesforceOwnerUserKey}            |
	| Salesforce Project Key                 | ${staticSalesforceProjectKey}              |
	| Start Day                              | ${staticStartDay}                          |
	| Start Month                            | ${staticStartMonth}                        |
	| Start Year                             | ${staticStartYear}                         |
	| Subscription Level                     | Platinum                                   |
	| Version Number                         | 7.1                                        |
	And I wait for "10" seconds
	And I generate static start and end dates
	And I generate static full start and end dates
	And I update a product purchase on koroneiki made by the account "Korpro - ${staticCompanyName}" for the product "A Liferay DXP Product" to have the following values
	| End Date                | ${staticEndDate}         | |
	| Original End Date       | ${staticOriginalEndDate} | |
	| Perpetual               | false                    | |
	| Start Date              | ${staticStartDate}       | |
	| Status                  | Approved                 | |
	And I update a product purchase on koroneiki made by the account "Korpro - ${staticCompanyName}" for the product "Platinum Subscription" to have the following values
	| End Date                | ${staticEndDate}         | |
	| Original End Date       | ${staticOriginalEndDate} | |
	| Perpetual               | false                    | |
	| Start Date              | ${staticStartDate}       | |
	| Status                  | Approved                 | |
	And I create a product consumption for an account with the name "Korpro - ${staticCompanyName}" and the product "A Liferay DXP Product" on koroneiki with the following values
	| Product Field and Value | additionalProp1 | propertyValue1 |
	| Product Field and Value | additionalProp2 | propertyValue2 |
	| Product Field and Value | additionalProp3 | propertyValue3 |
	And I log into the provisioning homepage as "test@liferay.com" with password "kwSgiajslgb7ecsD"
	And I search the accounts page using the keyword "Korpro"
	And I click on the account with the name "Korpro - ${staticCompanyName}" on the provisioning index
	Then I should be able to view the product under the "Active" tab with the name "A Liferay DXP Product" and the following values on the account details page
	| Name             | A Liferay DXP Product                         |
	| Support Life     | ${staticFullStartDate} - ${staticFullEndDate} |
	| Next Term Starts | false                                         |
	| Provisioned      | 1                                             |
	| Purchased        | 1                                             |
	| Status           | ACTIVE                                        |
	And I should be able to view the product under the "Active" tab with the name "Platinum Subscription" and the following values on the account details page
	| Name             | Platinum Subscription                         |
	| Support Life     | ${staticFullStartDate} - ${staticFullEndDate} |
	| Next Term Starts | false                                         |
	| Provisioned      | 0                                             |
	| Purchased        | 1                                             |
	| Status           | ACTIVE                                        |
	When I click on the "Inactive" tab
	Then I should not be able to view the product under the "Inactive" tab with the name "A Liferay DXP Product" on the account details page
	Then I should not be able to view the product under the "Inactive" tab with the name "Platinum Subscription" on the account details page
	When I click on the "All" tab
	Then I should be able to view the product under the "All" tab with the name "A Liferay DXP Product" and the following values on the account details page
	| Name             | A Liferay DXP Product                         |
	| Support Life     | ${staticFullStartDate} - ${staticFullEndDate} |
	| Next Term Starts | false                                         |
	| Provisioned      | 1                                             |
	| Purchased        | 1                                             |
	| Status           | ACTIVE                                        |
	And I should be able to view the product under the "All" tab with the name "Platinum Subscription" and the following values on the account details page
	| Name             | Platinum Subscription                         |
	| Support Life     | ${staticFullStartDate} - ${staticFullEndDate} |
	| Next Term Starts | false                                         |
	| Provisioned      | 0                                             |
	| Purchased        | 1                                             |
	| Status           | ACTIVE                                        |

Scenario: View future subscription
	Testing the ability to create a platinum subcription in Dossiera and updating the subscription to be later in the future before viewing the subscription in the provisioning account details page 

	Given I generate several static variables for Provisioning
	And I generate a provisioning company name
	And I generate a provisioning project name
	And I publish a project with no partner RabbitMQ message on sandbox with routing key "dossiera.provisioning.create" with the following values
	| Account Name                           | Korpro - ${staticCompanyName}              |
	| Address City                           | Diamond Bar                                |
	| Address Country                        | United States                              |
	| Address Postal Code                    | 91765                                      |
	| Address Region                         | California                                 |
	| Address Street                         | 456 Fake Street                            |
	| Contact Email Address                  | pro.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken       |
	| Contact First Name                     | PRO                                        |
	| Contact Last Name                      | Koroneiki1                                 |
	| Contact Role                           | Liferay Account Customer Role              |
	| Dossiera Account Key                   | ${staticDossieraAccountKey}                |
	| Dossiera Address Key 1                 | ${staticDossieraAddressKey1}               |
	| Dossiera Address Key 2                 | ${staticDossieraAddressKey2}               |
	| Dossiera Contact Key                   | ${staticDossieraContactKey}                |
	| Dossiera Project Key                   | ${staticDossieraProjectKey}                |
	| End Day                                | ${staticEndDay}                            |
	| End Month                              | ${staticEndMonth}                          |
	| End Year                               | ${staticEndYear}                           |
	| Industry                               | Automotive                                 |
	| Owner Email Address                    | pro.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken       |
	| Owner First Name                       | PRO                                        |
	| Owner Last Name                        | Koroneiki1                                 |
	| Partner First Line Support             | false                                      |
	| Product Type                           | New                                        |
	| Product Name                           | A Liferay DXP Product                      |
	| Project Name                           | Korpro - ${staticProjectName}              |
	| Renewal                                | false                                      |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Key             | ${staticSalesforceOpportunityKey}          |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Line Item Key 1 | ${staticSalesforceOpportunityLineItemKey1} |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Line Item Key 2 | ${staticSalesforceOpportunityLineItemKey2} |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Sold By         | Liferay US                                 |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Stage Name      | Closed Won                                 |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Territory       | United States                              |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Type            | New Business                               |
	| Salesforce Owner User Key              | ${staticSalesforceOwnerUserKey}            |
	| Salesforce Project Key                 | ${staticSalesforceProjectKey}              |
	| Start Day                              | ${staticStartDay}                          |
	| Start Month                            | ${staticStartMonth}                        |
	| Start Year                             | ${staticStartYear}                         |
	| Subscription Level                     | Platinum                                   |
	| Version Number                         | 7.1                                        |
	And I wait for "10" seconds
	And I generate future static start and end dates
	And I generate future static full start and end dates
	And I update a product purchase on koroneiki made by the account "Korpro - ${staticCompanyName}" for the product "A Liferay DXP Product" to have the following values
	| End Date                | ${staticFutureEndDate}         | |
	| Original End Date       | ${staticFutureOriginalEndDate} | |
	| Perpetual               | false                          | |
	| Start Date              | ${staticFutureStartDate}       | |
	| Status                  | Approved                       | |
	And I update a product purchase on koroneiki made by the account "Korpro - ${staticCompanyName}" for the product "Platinum Subscription" to have the following values
	| End Date                | ${staticFutureEndDate}         | |
	| Original End Date       | ${staticFutureOriginalEndDate} | |
	| Perpetual               | false                          | |
	| Start Date              | ${staticFutureStartDate}       | |
	| Status                  | Approved                       | |
	And I create a product consumption for an account with the name "Korpro - ${staticCompanyName}" and the product "A Liferay DXP Product" on koroneiki with the following values
	| Product Field and Value | additionalProp1 | propertyValue1 |
	| Product Field and Value | additionalProp2 | propertyValue2 |
	| Product Field and Value | additionalProp3 | propertyValue3 |
	And I log into the provisioning homepage as "test@liferay.com" with password "kwSgiajslgb7ecsD"
	And I search the accounts page using the keyword "Korpro"
	And I click on the account with the name "Korpro - ${staticCompanyName}" on the provisioning index
	Then I should not be able to view the product under the "Active" tab with the name "A Liferay DXP Product" on the account details page
	And I should not be able to view the product under the "Active" tab with the name "Platinum Subscription" on the account details page
	When I click on the "Inactive" tab
	Then I should be able to view the product under the "Inactive" tab with the name "A Liferay DXP Product" and the following values on the account details page
	| Name             | A Liferay DXP Product                                     |
	| Support Life     | ${staticFullFutureStartDate} - ${staticFullFutureEndDate} |
	| Next Term Starts | false                                                     |
	| Provisioned      | 1                                                         |
	| Purchased        | 1                                                         |
	| Status           | UNACTIVATED                                               |
	And I should be able to view the product under the "Inactive" tab with the name "Platinum Subscription" and the following values on the account details page
	| Name             | Platinum Subscription                                     |
	| Support Life     | ${staticFullFutureStartDate} - ${staticFullFutureEndDate} |
	| Next Term Starts | false                                                     |
	| Provisioned      | 0                                                         |
	| Purchased        | 1                                                         |
	| Status           | UNACTIVATED                                               |
	When I click on the "All" tab
	Then I should be able to view the product under the "All" tab with the name "A Liferay DXP Product" and the following values on the account details page
	| Name             | A Liferay DXP Product                                     |
	| Support Life     | ${staticFullFutureStartDate} - ${staticFullFutureEndDate} |
	| Next Term Starts | false                                                     |
	| Provisioned      | 1                                                         |
	| Purchased        | 1                                                         |
	| Status           | UNACTIVATED                                               |
	And I should be able to view the product under the "All" tab with the name "Platinum Subscription" and the following values on the account details page
	| Name             | Platinum Subscription                                     |
	| Support Life     | ${staticFullFutureStartDate} - ${staticFullFutureEndDate} |
	| Next Term Starts | false                                                     |
	| Provisioned      | 0                                                         |
	| Purchased        | 1                                                         |
	| Status           | UNACTIVATED                                               |

